nt so far, with no clear tailwind for either party", "Republican edge visible in Montana's 2026 Senate and House contests"], "rationale": "Montana's ten-point Republican lean and the absence of any polling or ratings pointing to a closer presidential race keep this firmly in Republican territory. With no incumbent running and a neutral national environment, there is little specific evidence to move the estimate away from the state's fundamentals.", "watch": "A decisive national swing toward either party in 2028, or the first Montana-specific presidential polls showing a materially different race, would be the clearest reason to revise.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No expert ratings published yet; forecast rests on fundamentals and polls.", "New or vacant seat with no expert ratings; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Montana remains one of the most Republican-leaning states in presidential politics, with a partisan lean of roughly ten points to the right. No incumbent is on the ballot in 2028, and no public general-election polls of the presidential race have been conducted in the state. The national environment appears roughly neutral so far, offering neither party a clear tailwind.\n\nDownballot signals point the same direction: outside groups are heavily involved in Montana's Senate race, and independent observers there see a sizable Republican edge. With no polling, expert ratings, or fundraising data specific to the presidential contest, the estimate rests on the state's underlying lean. That leaves wide uncertainty about the exact margin, but a clear Republican favorite.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.1274, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.185, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.1774, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1746, "margin": -10.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.1726, "margin": -10.